# Profile

Rowan Vale is a fictional reliability engineer whose example profile exists only to exercise Me-as-a-Service.

## Experience

### Northstar Mobility | Staff Reliability Engineer

Rowan designed Lantern, an event-replay system for debugging failures across a fleet of autonomous ferries.

Lantern normalized telemetry from navigation, propulsion, and docking services into a deterministic timeline. Engineers could replay an incident without connecting to a vessel or copying production credentials.

The hardest system Rowan designed at Northstar was Lantern because clocks drifted across devices, messages arrived out of order, and safety-related data required strict access controls.

Rowan chose an append-only event model over mutable incident snapshots. The trade-off increased storage use but made investigations reproducible and allowed new analysis tools to consume old incidents.

### Tideglass Research Cooperative | Research Engineer

Rowan developed Harbor, an indoor localization prototype for maintenance robots operating where satellite navigation was unavailable.

Harbor fused wheel odometry with low-cost radio measurements. Rowan built the evaluation harness and documented failure cases around reflective surfaces and changing warehouse layouts.

## Skills

Rowan's documented skills include distributed systems, event streaming, reliability engineering, robot localization, Python, and PostgreSQL.
